    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "[Ibis](https://ibis-project.org) is a newer framework that uses duckdb as a\n",
        "backend by default, and its API is a mix between duckdb and dplyr."
      ],
      "id": "a0bd20d4"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import ibis\n",
        "from ibis import _\n",
        "\n",
        "ibis.options.interactive = True\n",
        "\n",
        "import pandas as pd"
      ],
      "id": "25fec498",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "`_` in Ibis is a special variable that refers to the last expression evaluated.\n",
        "This is useful for chaining operations or for using the result of the last\n",
        "expression in subsequet operations. By default, ibis defers execution until you\n",
        "call `execute()` (much like dask). Using the above code\n",
        "`ibis.options.interactive = True` makes it so that expressions are immediately\n",
        "executed when displayed. As the text implies, its useful for interactive\n",
        "exploration.\n",
        "\n",
        "Below is the equivalent code in both pandas and ibis for the `purchases.csv`\n",
        "example dataset.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.columns}\n",
        "::::: {.column width=\"50%\"}"
      ],
      "id": "4059bf25"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "purchases = \"/Users/eo/Downloads/purchases.csv\"\n",
        "pandas_df = pd.read_csv(purchases)\n",
        "pandas_df.head(10)"
      ],
      "id": "62e67522",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        ":::::\n",
        "\n",
        "::::: {.column width=\"50%\"}"
      ],
      "id": "42cc714d"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "df = ibis.read_csv(purchases)\n",
        "df.head(10)"
      ],
      "id": "c49712b4",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        ":::::\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "How much do we sell..? Lets take the total sum"
      ],
      "id": "9805be1e"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "pandas_df[\"amount\"].sum()"
      ],
      "id": "42250df2",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "df[\"amount\"].sum().execute()"
      ],
      "id": "126c99a0",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "So that's why they wanted it by country! Pandas:"
      ],
      "id": "3ad0454d"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "(pandas_df.groupby(\"country\").agg(total=(\"amount\", \"sum\")).reset_index())"
      ],
      "id": "57e34aad",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Ibis:"
      ],
      "id": "d12e4101"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# NOTE: The .order_by() function is optional, only to align with the pandas\n",
        "# output.\n",
        "(df.group_by(\"country\").aggregate(totals=_.amount.sum()).order_by(\"country\"))"
      ],
      "id": "9cc93762",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    }
